message:
{{#is_alert}}Ferry has not mirrored {{repo.name}} from GitHub to Forgejo for over 1 hour (stale critical = 12 x poll interval, assuming the default 300 s poll interval). The Forgejo copy is falling behind.

First check: open the "Ferry: GitHub to Forgejo mirror" dashboard, filter `repo` to {{repo.name}}, and read the error kinds widget. Then search logs with `service:ferry status:error @repo:{{repo.name}}` for the latest failure.

If the error kind is `dest_unmanaged`, the `ferry-mirror` topic is missing from the Forgejo repository. That is the per-repository stop switch: ferry refuses to write until the topic is restored. If the pause was intentional, remove the entry from the allowlist and resolve this alert by hand. Otherwise restore the topic; a pod restart retries immediately, otherwise the next attempt can be up to 60 minutes away.{{/is_alert}}

{{#is_warning}}Ferry has not mirrored {{repo.name}} for over 30 minutes. If the next sync succeeds this clears by itself. Check the "Ferry: GitHub to Forgejo mirror" dashboard for the error kind on this repository.{{/is_warning}}

{{#is_recovery}}{{repo.name}} synced successfully again.{{/is_recovery}}
